The primary function of the peptide hormone renin in the human body is to initiate the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system (RAAS), which regulates blood pressure and electrolyte balance. Specifically, renin triggers a cascade of reactions that ultimately lead to the production of angiotensin II, a potent vasoconstrictor that increases blood pressure.
