What is the duration of a semibreve and a crochet in musical notation?
Based on the provided context, a semibreve (also known as a whole note) is a musical note that lasts for four beats in time, which is the whole measure (or bar). A crotchet (also known as a quarter note) is a note played for one quarter of the duration of a whole note (or semibreve), which means it lasts for one beat.

So, to summarize:

* A semibreve (whole note) lasts for 4 beats.
* A crotchet (quarter note) lasts for 1 beat.
