What is the definition of a semibreve and a crochet in musical notation?
A semibreve is a musical note represented by a hollow oval note head and no note stem, and its length is equal to four beats in time, that is the whole measure (or bar). 

A crochet is a note played for one quarter of the duration of a whole note (or semibreve), and it is also known as a quarter note in American musical notation.
